Types of outliers
There are different types of outliers 
univariate (in a single attribute); 
multivariate (occurs in the joint combination of two or 
more attributes); 
global outlier (with respect to the whole data set; 
contextual outlier (temperature in a region – we need 
some knowledge about the seasonal characteristics of 
that region); 
collective outlier (a subset of the data is significantly 
different than the rest of the data set)
